"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[57194],{42690:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"Apply","desc":"Sets the weather over `biomeId` at `weight` (0 = biome only, 1 = full weather).","params":[{"name":"biomeId","desc":"Name of a folder in `ReplicatedStorage.Biome`; missing \u2192 `Normal`.","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"weight","desc":"0..1, default 1.","lua_type":"number?"},{"name":"values","desc":"Weather table to use instead of `LeviathanConfig.Weather`.","lua_type":"table?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":160,"path":"src/ReplicatedStorage/SharedModules/LeviathanWeather.luau"}},{"name":"Preview","desc":"Studio edit-mode preview: switches Lighting to `biomeId` and applies the weather\\nfrom a fresh copy of `LeviathanConfig` (the command bar keeps the first `require`\\nof a module, so plain `Apply` would miss config edits). Weight 0 = biome only.","params":[{"name":"biomeId","desc":"","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"weight","desc":"0..1, default 1.","lua_type":"number?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":220,"path":"src/ReplicatedStorage/SharedModules/LeviathanWeather.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"LeviathanWeather","desc":"The Leviathan visit weather (storm sky, thick fog, dim light) blended over one\\nbiome. No screen filter: the train keeps its own colours. It reads the biome\'s own\\nvalues from `ReplicatedStorage.Biome.<Id>` (the `Atmosphere` and `Sky` templates and\\nthe Lighting attributes) and mixes them toward `LeviathanConfig.Weather` (with\\n`PerBiome` overrides). It edits the live `Lighting` Atmosphere, `Brightness`,\\n`OutdoorAmbient`, `Ambient` and `ExposureCompensation`. Past `SkySwapAt` it swaps\\nthe biome Sky for one named `LeviathanWeatherSky`; below it the biome Sky comes back.\\nAtmosphere fog only thickens with distance, so `workspace.LeviathanMist` (an\\ninvisible part with a particle emitter) rolls mist clouds across the train. The fog\\nis a short sight wall (old Silent Hill style), so a `Highlight` named\\n`WeatherSilhouette` keeps the Leviathan a dark shape through it.\\n`LeviathanWeatherController` calls it every frame during a visit.\\n\\nStudio preview from the command bar (the Clone loads the newest code; re-run after\\neach edit; run it with `.Preview(\\"Normal\\", 0)` before you save):\\n```lua\\nlocal m = game.ReplicatedStorage.SharedModules local c = m.LeviathanWeather:Clone() c.Parent = m require(c).Preview(\\"Void\\") c:Destroy()\\n```","source":{"line":24,"path":"src/ReplicatedStorage/SharedModules/LeviathanWeather.luau"}}')}}]);